-  public java.util.List<org.springframework.validation.ObjectError> getAllErrors();
+  public java.util.List getAllErrors();
```

2. `version-diff/api-diffs/org/springframework/validation/AbstractPropertyBindingResult.diff`
```diff
-  private org.springframework.core.convert.ConversionService conversionService;
-  public void initConversion(org.springframework.core.convert.ConversionService);
-  public java.beans.PropertyEditor findEditor(java.lang.String, java.lang.Class);
```

Supporting Evidence:
- The validation hierarchy changes (AbstractBindingResult → AbstractPropertyBindingResult → BeanPropertyBindingResult) show multiple breaking API changes
- Removal of generic type parameters would cause ClassCastExceptions in modern Java code
- The conversion service disappearance breaks type conversion during property binding
- Missing auto-grow flag in BeanPropertyBindingResult indicates regression in nested path handling

Open Questions:
- Was 2.5.6.SEC01 intentionally meant to be API-incompatible with 3.x?
- Are there migration guides indicating these breaking changes were expected?
- Could this be a misversioned artifact where 2.5.6.SEC01 was accidentally used instead of a 3.x patch?
```

